Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *iOS Software Engineer* position on Snap's Messaging team. I bring more than three years of professional software development experience, an MS in Computer Science from Pace University, and a record of shipping real-time, consumer-facing systems where reliability, latency, performance, and clear operational signals matter.

At Sperse, I designed and shipped a real-time visual workflow experience used within a platform serving 10,000+ users. I paired React Flow and TypeScript with Temporal and Redis to provide live progress notifications, durable execution, and recovery for asynchronous workflows. I also improved a distributed CRM platform through secure request routing, retries, and resumable execution, then instrumented production workflows with OpenTelemetry trace-based evaluations and CI/CD checks for latency, accuracy, and safety. That combination of async/concurrent programming, performance tuning, testing, and observability maps directly to building fast, reliable messaging experiences and investigating incidents or hotfixes.

Earlier at Qualitest, I built a Java and Spring Boot storage service that delivered uploads and downloads through expiring signed URLs across Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO. I also orchestrated asynchronous jobs across 100K+ weekly executions with AWS Step Functions and Lambda, improving error recovery through retries and observable failure states. This work required close collaboration across application, data, and infrastructure boundaries—the same discipline needed to partner with product, design, and backend teams while maintaining code quality in a large-scale codebase.

Snap's mission to empower people to express themselves, live in the moment, learn about the world, and have fun together is especially compelling in a role centered on communication between friends and family. I would bring a kind, smart, and creative approach to the Messaging team: acting on hard reliability problems, making evidence-based decisions from instrumentation, and learning quickly as features move from roadmap to production. I would welcome the opportunity to help improve chat and media delivery experiences for Snapchatters and can be reached at #ph or #eml.

#cv_ending()
